// The attempts sets (0.6.6): requests to try or change something, run in real Claude Code sessions to capture how
// Claude words its reply when the attempt fails and, as controls, when it works. Captured with
// scripts/capture-stops.mjs. Three projects are the dev set (eval/attempts-dev-sessions.jsonl, labelled as
// eval/attempts-dev.jsonl) and two are held out (eval/attempts-heldout-sessions.jsonl, labelled as
// eval/attempts-heldout-captured.jsonl): nobody who tuned the change read their replies. A second held-out set,
// eval/attempts-heldout.jsonl, is written, in four other projects.
//
// The projects are eval/attempts/projects/<name>: five small programs built for this, with nothing to install. Every
// trap was done by hand in a copy of its project before any session ran, twice, by a builder and by a second checker:
//   attempt-fail  the thing asked for really fails here, for the cause in `why` ("fails"), or fails at first and a
//                 quick fix makes it work ("fixable": what a session then does is open)
//   attempt-work  it really works
//   decision      a real decision, rule or preference given as an instruction that is simply carried out
//   ordinary      a question about the code, a bug report for a bug planted in the project, a to-do for later
// No prompt says that an attempt will fail, or why. A row's label comes from what the session's reply says happened,
// not from the kind here: a session may decline to try, or find a way through.
//
// Sessions: every case once with Claude Code's default model; every failing trap twice more, on claude-fable-5-1 and
// on one of two other pinned models in turn; every second working trap once more on a pinned model. Models word a
// failure differently, and the default changes from hour to hour. Each captured row records the model that served it.
export const SET = "attempts";

/** The two projects whose captured sessions are held out. */
export const HELDOUT_PROJECTS = ["quillcase", "relaydesk"];

/** The memory lines each project already has (the rows' `existing`). */
export const EXISTING = {
  ledgerline: [{"id":"le1","kind":"decision","text":"The report is plain text with no colours or box-drawing characters, because it is pasted into emails."},{"id":"le2","kind":"constraint","text":"The ledger in test/fixtures is made up; a real bank export must never be committed."},{"id":"le3","kind":"preference","text":"Error messages for a bad row start with the line number, as in \"line 12: not an amount\"."}],
  pagewright: [{"id":"pa1","kind":"decision","text":"Each page is written to <slug>/index.html, not <slug>.html, so links end in a slash and carry no file extension."},{"id":"pa2","kind":"constraint","text":"Generated pages must not load anything from another host (no CDN scripts, fonts or styles), because the site has to open straight from disk."},{"id":"pa3","kind":"architecture","text":"markdown.py and pages.py do no file I/O; only build.py and config.py read or write files."}],
  gridwatch: [{"id":"gr1","kind":"decision","text":"Station ids such as st-04 are the key in readings and alerts; a station's display name is never written to alerts.jsonl"},{"id":"gr2","kind":"constraint","text":"gridwatch runs on the site gateway boxes, which cannot reach a package registry, so it takes no npm dependencies"},{"id":"gr3","kind":"preference","text":"Test names are written as plain sentences about behaviour, never as function names"}],
  quillcase: [{"id":"qu1","kind":"decision","text":"diff_lines compares lines exactly, trailing whitespace included; callers strip first if they want it ignored."},{"id":"qu2","kind":"constraint","text":"The test suite has to stay offline and finish in a couple of seconds, so golden inputs are kept short."},{"id":"qu3","kind":"preference","text":"Docstrings stay on one line; longer explanations belong in the README."}],
  relaydesk: [{"id":"re1","kind":"decision","text":"Job payloads are stored as opaque JSON and relaydesk never validates them; each handler checks its own input."},{"id":"re2","kind":"constraint","text":"relaydesk must work on a machine with no network access: nothing in it may open a socket or fetch anything."},{"id":"re3","kind":"preference","text":"Error messages are lower-case with no trailing period, in the form `no such job: <id>`."}],
};

